   "date": "2019-01-10T00:17:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: Questions regarding TMT analysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">Farhad,</span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For your questions: </span></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">1. Why </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">normalization</span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> is to be applied after summarization?</span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There are mainly two reasons. First, the large percentage of missing </span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">peptide identifications</span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> across LC-MS runs in TMT experiment makes it difficult to do</span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"> normalization on peptides before summarization. Second, based on our evaluation, normalization after summarization shows a better testing performance than </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">normalization before summarization.</span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">2. What is the difference between summarisation method “msstats” and “ MedianPolish”? In method msstats the summary method is still TMP!</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">You are right that </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">“msstats” and “ MedianPolish” both use TMP as summarization methods. But </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">“msstats”</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">  has one additional step which imputes the missing values within each LC-MS run. </span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">3. The vignette of the package is not explaining the statistical concepts behind TMT analysis. Would you please address me to some resources on this regard? </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">We are preparing the manuscript about MSstatsTMT package. We will update the citation information in MSstatsTMT webpage as it comes out.</span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">4. In PDtoMSstatsTMTFormat, the the parameter “summaryforMultipleRows” is set to sum by default. Shouldn’t it be applied after normalisation?</span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">The parameter “summaryforMultipleRows”  is used to deal with the case that one peptide matches with multiple spectra.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"> MSstatsTMT </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">selects the intensity from the best PSM as the final peptide intensity. Then </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">MSstatsTMT summarizes the peptide intensities into protein intensity.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">5. Normalization between MS runs will be done by using Norm channels. But don&#39;t we also need to normalise between channels after combining the fractions (or before that)?</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">The aim of normalization is to remove the technical </span><span style=\"color:rgb(84,84,84);font-family:Roboto,arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">variability</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"> in TMT data. And the advantage of TMT experiment is that all the samples in one MS run suffer the same technical biases. So we only do normalization between runs. </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">Best,</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\">Ting</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"> </span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
